.TH UNIWIFI 1 "October 2026" "uniwifi 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uniwifi \- zero-touch captive portal auto-login background daemon for Fedora Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uniwifi
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uniwifi
is an autonomous background daemon engineered for Fedora Linux that detects captive
portals upon network connection, network interface flappings, or systemd-logind sleep/resume,
and automatically submits credentials stored securely in the system keyring.
.PP
Passphrases and credentials are never stored on disk or logged; they are stored encrypted
via the FreeDesktop Secret Service API (GNOME Keyring / libsecret).

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB--json\fR] [\fB-v\fR]
Checks current internet connectivity and prints captive portal redirection URL if intercepted.
.TP
.B setup \fR[\fB--check\fR] [\fB--delete\fR] [\fB-u \fIUSERNAME\fR]
Interactively prompts for university username and password and stores them in the OS keyring.
.TP
.B login \fR[\fB--browser\fR] [\fB--url \fIURL\fR] [\fB--dry-run\fR] [\fB--password-stdin\fR]
Performs an immediate one-shot login attempt against the captive portal.
.TP
.B run \fR[\fB--foreground\fR]
Launches the long-running async daemon listening for D-Bus signals from NetworkManager and systemd-logind.
.TP
.B service \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Controls the systemd user service unit. Subcommands include:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinstall\fR: Installs the unit to ~/.config/systemd/user/uniwifi.service.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBuninstall\fR: Removes the user service unit.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstatus\fR: Inspects active state and PID.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstart\fR, \fBstop\fR, \fBrestart\fR: Controls service execution.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBenable\fR, \fBdisable\fR: Toggles auto-start upon user login.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlogs\fR: Queries journalctl user logs.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcat\fR: Displays installed unit file content.
.RE
.TP
.B doctor \fR[\fB--json\fR] [\fB--fix\fR]
Runs comprehensive diagnostic self-tests covering Python runtime, Secret Service keyring,
system D-Bus, notification daemon, file permissions, and systemd service state.
.TP
.B config \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manages the TOML configuration file. Subcommands include: \fBshow\fR, \fBinit\fR, \fBpath\fR, and \fBaudit\fR.
.TP
.B recon \fR[\fB--json\fR] [\fB--probe\fR]
Performs network reconnaissance on active Wi-Fi adapters and extracts portal login form structures.
.TP
.B events \fR[\fB--timeout \fISECONDS\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Streams live system D-Bus signals from NetworkManager and systemd-logind for troubleshooting.
.TP
.B notify \fR[\fB--kind \fIKIND\fR] [\fB--title \fITITLE\fR] [\fB--body \fIBODY\fR]
Sends a test desktop notification via libnotify.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Enable verbose debug output.
.TP
.B --version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B --help
Show help message and exit.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/uniwifi/config.toml
Main user configuration file. Must have mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/uniwifi.service
User systemd unit definition.
.TP
.I /usr/share/uniwifi/config.example.toml
System default example configuration.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General operational error or verification failure.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration syntax or validation error.
.TP
.B 3
Credentials missing or keyring inaccessible.
.TP
.B 4
Security rejection (insecure HTTP or untrusted host).
.TP
.B 130
Process terminated by SIGINT / KeyboardInterrupt.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uniwifi.toml (5),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR NetworkManager (8),
.BR gnome-keyring (1)
